verses.text:
“Before I formed you in the belly I knew you,
and before you came out from the womb I set you apart;
a prophet to the nations I appointed you.”

Yet Yahweh answered me,
“Say not, ‘A youth am I’;
for wherever I send you, there you must go,
and whatever I bid you, that you must speak.

Holy was Israel to Yahweh,
the firstfruits of his harvest;
all who devoured him were held guilty;
disaster came upon them,’ declares Yahweh.”

And I brought you into a land of orchards,{d}
to eat its fruit and its good things;
but you came in and defiled my land,
and my heritage you made an abomination.

The priests never asked, ‘Where is Yahweh?’
Those who wield the law knew me not;
the shepherds{e} rebelled against me;
the prophets spoke by Baal{f}
and pursued what brings no gain.

Over him the young lions have roared;
they have lifted up their voice.
They have made his land a waste;
his cities are burned, without inhabitant.

And now, what have you to do with the road to Egypt,
to drink the waters of the Shihor?{m}
Or what have you to do with the road to Assyria,
to drink the waters of the River?{n}

Your own evil will discipline you,
and your turnings away will rebuke you.
Know then and see that it is evil and bitter
for you to forsake Yahweh your God;
the dread of me is not in you,”
declares the Lord Yahweh of Armies.{o}

“How can you say, ‘I am not defiled;
after the Baals I have not gone’?
See your way in the valley;{p}
know what you have done—
a swift young she-camel
running crisscross on her paths,

Where then are those gods you made for yourself?
Up with them, if they can rescue you
when trouble comes;
for your gods have grown as many
as your towns, O Judah.{q}

O generation, you—see the word of Yahweh!
Have I been a wilderness to Israel,
or a land of thick darkness?{r}
Why do my people say, ‘We roam free;
we will come to you no more’?

Even in your skirts is found
the blood of the guiltless poor;
not as housebreakers did you find them.{s}
Yet in spite of all this

From there also you shall go out
with your hands upon your head;{t}
for Yahweh has rejected those in whom you trust,
and you shall not prosper through them.

Go and proclaim these words toward the north, and say,
‘Return, faithless Israel,’ declares Yahweh;
‘I will not let my face fall upon you in anger,
for faithful am I,’ declares Yahweh;
‘I will not keep anger forever.

Let us lie down in our shame,
and let our disgrace cover us;
for against Yahweh our God we have sinned,
we and our fathers,
from our youth even to this day,
and we have not obeyed the voice of Yahweh our God.”

Raise a signal toward Zion;
flee for safety; do not stand still,
for I am bringing disaster from the north,
and a great destruction.

Up from his thicket the lion has gone,
the ravager of nations is on the march;
out from his place he has come
to turn your land into a waste;
your towns shall lie in ruins, empty of people.

My bowels, my bowels!{d} I writhe in pain!
O the walls of my heart!
My heart moans within me;
I cannot keep silent,
for the sound of the ram’s horn you have heard, O my soul,
the alarm of war.

For thus says Yahweh:
“A desolation shall the whole land be;
yet a full end I will not make.

Because of this the land shall mourn,
and the sky above grow black;
for I have spoken it, I have determined it;
I will not relent, nor will I draw back.”

At the noise of horseman and archer
every city flees;
they go into thickets;
they climb among the rocks;
every city is forsaken,
and no man dwells in them.

O Yahweh, do not your eyes look for faithfulness?
You struck them, but they felt no grief;
you consumed them, but they refused to accept correction.
Harder than rock they made their faces;
they refused to turn back.

Then I said, “Surely these are only the poor;
they act foolishly,
for they know not Yahweh’s way,
the judgment of their God.

I will get me to the great ones
and speak with them,
for they know Yahweh’s way,
the judgment of their God.”
But these too had all alike shattered the yoke;
they had snapped the bonds.

Therefore a lion from the forest shall slay them;
a wolf of the desert plains shall ravage them;
a leopard keeps watch over their towns;
whoever goes out of them shall be torn in pieces,
because their transgressions are many,
mighty their acts of turning away.

Shall I not punish them for these things?” declares Yahweh;
“and on a nation such as this
shall my soul not take vengeance?

The prophets shall turn to wind;
the word is not in them.
So be it done to them!”

Your crops and your bread they will devour;
your sons and daughters they will devour;
your sheep and cattle they will devour;
your vine and fig they will devour;
the walled towns you rely on
they will batter down with the sword.

Will you not fear me?’ declares Yahweh.
‘Before me will you not tremble?
I placed the sand as the bound of the sea,
a perpetual decree it cannot pass;
though its waves toss, they cannot prevail;
though they roar, they cannot pass over it.

For among my people are found wicked men;
they watch like fowlers who crouch;{e}
they set a trap;
men they catch.

Like a cage full of birds,
so are their houses full of deceit;
therefore they have become great and grown rich.

They have grown fat and sleek;
they also overpass in deeds of evil;
they plead not the cause, the cause of the fatherless, that they may prosper,
and the right of the needy they do not defend.

Shall I not punish them for these things?’ declares Yahweh;
‘and on a nation such as this
shall my soul not take vengeance?’

Herdsmen with their flocks will march on her;
round about her they will pitch their tents;
each will crop his own patch.

For thus says Yahweh of Armies:
“Hew down her trees;
cast up a siege mound against Jerusalem.
This is the city to be punished;
oppression is all within her.

As a cistern keeps its water cool,
so she keeps her evil cool and fresh;
outrage and havoc echo in her;
sickness and blows are before my face continually.

But I am full of the wrath of Yahweh;
I am weary of holding it in.
“Pour it out upon the child in the street,
and upon the gathering of young men together;
for husband with wife shall be taken,
the elder with him who is full of days.

Did they feel shame for the loathsome things they did?
Not the least shame did they feel;
blushing they never learned.
So they will go down with the fallen;
when I call them to account they will be overthrown,” Yahweh has said.

Thus says Yahweh:
“See, a people comes from the land of the north;
a great nation is stirred up from the farthest parts of the earth.

Bow and javelin they grip;
cruel are they, and show no mercy;
their voice roars like the sea;
upon horses they ride,
arrayed as a man for battle
against you, O daughter of Zion.”

We have heard the report of it;
our hands hang limp;
anguish has seized us,
pain as of a woman in labor.

Venture not into the countryside,
nor travel the highway,
for the foe bears a sword;
dread surrounds on all sides.{g}

They are all stubborn rebels,
going about with slander;
bronze and iron are they;
all of them deal corruptly.

The bellows blow fiercely;
the lead is consumed by the fire;{i}
in vain the refiner refines,
for the wicked are not drawn off.

The wise men are put to shame;
they are dismayed and caught;
see, they have rejected the word of Yahweh,
so what wisdom is in them?

Therefore I will give their wives to others,
their fields to new owners;
for from the least to the greatest
every one is greedy for unjust gain;
from prophet to priest
every one deals falsely.

They have healed the wound of the daughter of my people lightly,
saying, “Peace, peace,”
when there is no peace.{b}

Were they ashamed when they committed abomination?
No, they were not at all ashamed;
they knew not how to blush.
Therefore they shall fall among those who fall;
in the time of their punishment they shall stumble,’ says Yahweh.

‘I will surely gather them in,’{c} declares Yahweh;
‘there are no grapes on the vine,
nor figs on the fig tree;
even the leaf has withered,
and what I gave them passes away from them.’”{d}

Why are we sitting here?
Assemble! Let us enter the walled towns
and meet our end there;
for Yahweh our God has sentenced us to die
and made us drink water laced with poison,{e}
since against Yahweh we have sinned.

They bend their tongue like their bow;
falsehood and not faithfulness has grown strong in the land;
for they proceed from evil to evil,
and me they do not know, declares Yahweh.

Guard yourselves, each against his friend,
and rely on no brother;
for each brother is a heel-grabber,{b}
and each friend peddles slander.

Each one deceives his neighbor,
and no one speaks the truth;
they have taught their tongue to speak lies;
they weary themselves committing iniquity.

A death-dealing arrow is their tongue;
treachery is its speech;
with his lips a man greets his friend with “Peace,”
but inwardly he plots to waylay him.

Over the hills I will lift up weeping and lament,
and over the wilderness grazing lands a dirge,
for they are scorched, with none passing through,
and no sound of cattle is heard;
the birds of the sky as well as the beasts
have fled away and gone.

Thus says Yahweh of Armies:
“Consider, and call for the mourning women to come;
send for the skillful women to come;

let them hurry and lift a dirge over us,
till our eyes stream with tears
and our lashes drip with water.

They adorn it with silver and with gold;
they fasten it with nails and hammers
so that it cannot move.

They are like a scarecrow in a melon patch,{a}
mute and unable to talk;
they must be hauled about,
having no power to walk.
Have no fear of them,
for harm is beyond them,
and good is beyond them too.”

Beaten silver is brought from Tarshish,
and gold from Uphaz,{c}
the work of the craftsman and of the hands of the goldsmith;
their clothing is blue and purple;
they are all the work of skilled men.

He made the earth by his power;
he established the world by his wisdom,
and by his understanding stretched out the heavens.

Every man is stupid, without knowledge;
every goldsmith is put to shame by his idol,
for his molten images are falsehood,
and there is no breath in them.

Not like these is the Portion of Jacob,{e}
for he is the Maker of all things,
and Israel is the tribe of his inheritance;
Yahweh of Armies is his name.

My tent is destroyed,
and all my cords are broken;
my children have gone from me,
and they are not;
there is no one to spread my tent again
and to set up my curtains.

But I was like a docile lamb
led away to the butcher;
I did not know it was against me
they had hatched their plots:
“Let us destroy the tree with its sap;{f}
let us cut him off from the land of the living,
that his name may be remembered no more.”

“If runners on foot have tired you out,
how can you race against horses?
And if only in a quiet land you feel secure,{a}
what will you do in the Jordan’s jungle?{b}

“I have abandoned my house;
I have cast off my heritage;
I have handed the darling of my soul
into the grip of her enemies.

My heritage has turned on me
like a lion in the forest;
she has raised her voice against me;
therefore I hate her.

Is my heritage to me a speckled bird of prey?{c}
Are the birds of prey against her on every side?
Go, assemble all the beasts of the field;
bring them to devour.

Many shepherds have ruined my vineyard;
they have trampled my portion;
they have turned my pleasant portion
into a desolate wilderness.

Their great men dispatch their lads for water;
to the pits they go;
no water do they find;
back they come, their jars empty;
shamed and humiliated,
they muffle their heads.

The wild donkeys stand on the bare heights;
they pant for air like jackals;
their eyes fail
because there is no herbage.

“Though our iniquities testify against us,
act, O Yahweh, for your name’s sake;
for many are our turnings away;
against you have we sinned.

This is what Yahweh says of this people:
“So well have they loved to wander;
their feet they have not restrained;
therefore Yahweh does not accept them;
now he will remember their iniquity
and punish their sins.”

For your name’s sake, do not despise us;
bring no disgrace on the throne of your glory;
keep in mind your covenant with us, and annul it not.

And when they ask you, ‘Where shall we go?’ tell them, ‘This is what Yahweh says:
“Those for death, to death;
those for the sword, to the sword;
those for famine, to famine;
those for captivity, to captivity.”’

You have cast me off, declares Yahweh;
backward you keep going;
so I have stretched out my hand against you and destroyed you;
I am weary of relenting.

I have winnowed them with a winnowing fork
in the gates of the land;
I have bereaved them, I have destroyed my people;
from their ways they did not turn.

I have made their widows outnumber
the grains of sand by the sea;
upon the mother of the young warriors
I have brought a ravager at midday;
I have let alarm and dismay
drop on her without warning.

The mother of seven grows faint;
she gasps out her life;
her sun has set while daylight remained;
humiliated is she, and abashed.
Whoever of them survive I will hand to the sword
in their foes’ presence, declares Yahweh.”

Yahweh said, “Surely I will set you free for good;{b}
surely I will make the enemy plead with you
in the time of evil and in the time of distress.

Yahweh, you understand;
keep me in mind and come to my aid;
take revenge for me on those who hound me.
Do not, through your patience with them, snatch me away;
consider how for you I endure insult.

“Judah’s sin is engraved with a pen of iron;
with a point of diamond{a} it is etched
on the tablet of their heart
and on the horns of your altars,{b}

He will be like a tree set by the water,
that pushes out its roots toward the stream;
it has no fear when the heat arrives,
and its foliage stays lush;
in a year of drought it is not anxious,
and it never stops yielding fruit.”

More tortuous{e} than all else is the heart,
and desperately sick;
who can fathom it?

O Yahweh, Hope of Israel,
all who abandon you shall be put to shame;
those who turn from you{f} shall be written in the dust,
for they have abandoned Yahweh,
the spring of living water.

Heal me, O Yahweh, and I shall be healed;
save me, and I shall be saved,
for you are my praise.

But I have not pressed you to send calamity,{g}
nor have I longed for the day of disaster;
you know it.
What came from my lips
was open before your face.

Let my persecutors be put to shame, but not me;
let them be dismayed, but not me;
bring on them the day of calamity;
with double destruction destroy them!

Does the snow of Lebanon leave
the crags of the field?{b}
Are the cold flowing waters
from afar ever dried up?{c}

Yet my people have forgotten me;
to vapor they burn offerings;
they made them stumble in their ways,
the ancient roads,
to walk in bypaths,
not a highway built up,

Therefore hand their sons over to famine;
pour them out to the power of the sword;
let their wives become childless and widowed;
let their men be slain by death,
their young men struck by the sword in battle.

You enticed me, O Yahweh, and I was enticed;{c}
you overpowered me, and you prevailed.
I have become a laughingstock all day;
everyone mocks me.

But Yahweh stands by me like a fearsome champion;
so those who hound me will trip up;
they will not win.
Deeply disgraced they will be, because they fail;
an eternal dishonor, never to be forgotten.

I will call you to account as your deeds deserve, declares Yahweh;
I will light a fire in her forest,
and it will devour everything around her.’”

With a donkey’s burial he will be buried,
dragged off and flung out
beyond Jerusalem’s gates.”{e}

“Climb Lebanon and cry out;
in Bashan lift up your voice;
cry out from Abarim,{f}
for all your lovers are crushed.

So says Yahweh:
“Record this man as childless,
a man who will not prosper in his days;
for none of his offspring will succeed
in sitting on David’s throne
and ruling again in Judah.”{i}

For the land is full of adulterers;
because of the curse{d} the land mourns;
the pastures of the wilderness are dried up.
Their course is evil,
and their might is not right.

“Therefore their way will be to them
like slippery paths in the darkness;
they will be thrust down and fall there;
for I will bring calamity on them,
the year of their punishment,” declares Yahweh.

So says Yahweh of Armies:
“Do not listen to the words of the prophets who prophesy to you;
they are filling you with vapor.{e}
They speak a vision from their own heart,
not from the mouth of Yahweh.

“You, then, prophesy against them all these words, and say to them:
‘Yahweh roars from on high;
from his holy dwelling he utters his voice;
he roars mightily against his pasture;
a shout like those who tread grapes
he raises against all the inhabitants of the earth.

The tumult reaches to the ends of the earth,
for Yahweh has a lawsuit with the nations;
he enters into judgment with all flesh;
the wicked he gives over to the sword,
declares Yahweh.’

“Wail, you shepherds, and cry out;
roll in the dust, you lords of the flock,
for your days for slaughter have come,
and you will be scattered,{l}
and you will fall like a precious vessel.

“But you, fear not, O Jacob my servant, declares Yahweh,
and do not lose heart, O Israel;
for look, I will rescue you from far away,
your offspring from the land of their captivity.
Jacob will come home and be at rest, untroubled,
with none to make him afraid.

For beside you I stand, declares Yahweh, to deliver you;
an utter finish I will make of every nation
where I dispersed you,
yet you I will not utterly finish.
With fairness I will discipline you;
unpunished I will not let you go.{c}

“For so says Yahweh:
Your fracture cannot be mended;
your wound is past cure.

No one pleads your case;
for a sore there is remedy,
but no new flesh for you.{d}

All your lovers have forgotten you;
they do not seek you out;
for I struck you with an enemy’s blow,
the chastisement of a cruel one,
because your guilt is great,
because your sins are many.

“So says Yahweh:
Look, I will turn back the captivity of Jacob’s tents
and have compassion on his dwellings;
the city will be rebuilt on its mound,{f}
and the citadel will stand where it rightly belongs.

So says Yahweh:
“Favor in the wilderness was found
by a people escaped from the sword;
Israel went on its way to find rest.{a}

From far off Yahweh appeared to me:{b}
‘With a love of old ages I have loved you;
that is why I have drawn you on with steadfast kindness.

For so says Yahweh:
“Raise a ringing shout for Jacob with gladness;
cry aloud at the head of the nations;
make it heard, give praise, and say,
‘Save, Yahweh, your people,
the remnant of Israel!’

Weeping they shall come;
amid their supplications I will conduct them;
by brooks of water I will walk them,
along a straight track where none trips;
for to Israel I am father,
and Ephraim—my firstborn he is.

Then the virgin will rejoice in the dance,
young men and old together;
I will turn their mourning into gladness;
I will comfort them and give them joy in place of sorrow.

For after I had turned away, I repented;
after I was made to understand, I struck my thigh;
I was ashamed, and also humiliated,
for I bore the disgrace of my youth.’

Plant waymarks for yourself;
erect guideposts;
fix your thoughts on the causeway,
the route you once traveled.
Turn back, virgin Israel;
turn back to these towns of yours.

Harness the horses;
mount, you horsemen!
Take your stations in helmets;
polish the lances;
put on the coats of mail!

Why have I seen it?
They are panic-stricken, falling back;
their warriors are beaten down;
they have fled headlong
and do not look back—
terror on every side!{d} declares Yahweh.

Charge, you horses;
rage, you chariots!
Let the warriors march out:
Cush and Put who handle the shield,
the Ludim who handle and bend the bow.{e}

The nations have heard of your shame,
and your cry has filled the earth;
for warrior has stumbled against warrior;
together the two of them have fallen.”

“Declare it in Egypt, proclaim it in Migdol;
proclaim it in Memphis and in Tahpanhes;
say, ‘Take your stand and get ready,
for the sword devours all around you.’

Many he caused to totter;
one toppled onto another;
then they said, ‘Up! Back to our kin,
back to the country that bore us,
far from the sword of the oppressor.’

Her mercenaries too, there within her,
are like stall-fattened calves;
they as well wheel around and run, all at once;
they hold no ground;
for their day of disaster is upon them,
their hour of reckoning.

Her sound is like a serpent slithering away,{h}
for in force they march,
and with axes they come against her
like woodcutters.

“But you, fear not, O Jacob my servant,
and do not lose heart, O Israel;
for look, I will rescue you from far away,
your offspring from the land of their captivity.
Jacob will come home and be at rest, untroubled,
with none to make him afraid.

Shaven bald is Gaza;
Ashkelon struck dumb.
You leftovers of their lowland,{c}
how long will you slash at your flesh?

Concerning Moab.{a}
So says Yahweh of Armies, God of Israel:
“Woe to Nebo, for it is laid waste!
Kiriathaim is put to shame, it is captured;
the stronghold{b} is put to shame and shattered.

Moab’s renown is no more;
in Heshbon they plotted harm against her:{c}
‘Come, let us cut her off from being a nation!’
You too, O Madmen, will be struck dumb;
after you the sword will go.

The destroyer will come upon every town;
no town will escape;
the valley will perish, and the plateau be laid waste,
as Yahweh has said.

Give wings to Moab,{f}
for she must fly away;
her towns will become a desolation,
with none to dwell in them.

“At ease has Moab been from his youth,
settled on his dregs;
he has not been poured from vessel to vessel,
nor has he gone into exile;
so his flavor has stayed in him,
and his scent is unchanged.

Therefore look, days are coming, declares Yahweh,
when I will send him pourers who will pour him out;
they will empty his vessels
and smash their jars.{g}

“Make him drunk,
for he magnified himself against Yahweh;
let Moab wallow in his vomit,
and he too shall become a laughingstock.

I know his insolence, declares Yahweh;
his boasts are false,
his deeds are false.

Therefore I wail for Moab;
for all Moab I cry out;
for the men of Kir-heres{i} one moans.

Beyond the weeping for Jazer I weep for you,
vine of Sibmah!
Over the sea your shoots stretched out;
to Jazer’s sea{j} they extended;
onto your ripe summer fruit and your grape harvest
the ravager has pounced.

Gone, swept off, are glee and merriment
from the orchard land, from Moab’s land;
wine from the vats I have stopped;
no treader tramples with a cheer;
the cheer is no harvest cheer.

Therefore my heart moans for Moab like flutes,
and my heart moans like flutes for the men of Kir-heres;
therefore the riches they gained have perished.

For so says Yahweh:
“Look, one will swoop like an eagle
and spread his wings over Moab.{k}

Terror, pit, and trap{m}
are upon you, O inhabitant of Moab,
declares Yahweh.

“In the shadow of Heshbon
the fugitives stop, without strength;{n}
for fire has gone out from Heshbon,
a flame from the midst of Sihon;
it has consumed the forehead of Moab,
the crown of the sons of tumult.

Woe to you, O Moab!
The people of Chemosh are undone;
for your sons have been taken captive,
and your daughters into captivity.

Edom will become a horror;
everyone who passes by it will be appalled
and will hiss because of all its wounds.

As happened at the toppling of Sodom and Gomorrah with their adjoining towns, Yahweh says,
not one person will reside there;
no mortal will so much as camp in her.

About Damascus.
“Disgraced are Hamath and Arpad,
for an evil report has reached their ears;
they dissolve with dread; at the sea is turmoil;{j}
it can find no rest.

I will shatter Elam before their enemies,
before those who seek their life;
I will bring disaster upon them,
my fierce anger, declares Yahweh;
I will send the sword after them
until I have consumed them.

In Elam I will set up my seat of rule;
king and princes I will abolish thence,
is Yahweh’s utterance.

“Declare among the nations and proclaim it;
raise a signal flag, proclaim it, do not hide it;
say: ‘Babylon is captured,
Bel{b} is put to shame,
Merodach is shattered;
her images are put to shame,
her idols{c} are shattered.’

For from the north a people climbs up to attack her;
her country it will turn to waste,
with no one living there;
human and animal alike have bolted and vanished.

My people have been lost sheep;
their shepherds led them astray,
turning them loose on the mountains;
from mountain to hill they went;
they forgot their fold.

For look, I am stirring up and bringing against Babylon
an assembly of great nations from the land of the north;
they will array themselves against her;
from there she will be taken.
Their arrows are like a skilled{d} warrior’s,
who does not return empty-handed.

Raise a shout against her all around:
she has given her hand;{e}
her bulwarks have fallen;
her walls are thrown down.
For this is the vengeance of Yahweh:
take vengeance on her;
as she has done, do to her.

Cut off from Babylon the sower
and the one who wields the sickle in time of harvest;
because of the oppressor’s sword{f}
each will turn back to his own people,
and each will flee to his own land.

“Go up against the land of Merathaim,{g}
against it, and against the inhabitants of Pekod;
slay and devote them to destruction, declares Yahweh,
and do all that I have commanded you.

Close in on her from the remotest edge;
break open her storehouses;
heap her like sheaves, and put her under the ban;
leave her no remainder.

Call up bowmen to Babylon,
every one who draws the bow;
pitch camp on every side of her;
allow no one to slip out.
Pay her back for her conduct;
the way she acted, act toward her;
for against Yahweh she was insolent,
against Israel’s Holy One.

Look, I am against you, O Arrogance,{i}
declares Lord Yahweh of Armies,
for your day has come,
the time when I punish you.

“Yahweh of Armies says this:
Crushed are Israel’s people,
and Judah’s people along with them;
their captors all clutch them tight;
they will not release them.

Therefore desert creatures with jackals will dwell there,
and ostriches will dwell in her;
she will never again be inhabited
or settled from generation to generation.{l}

“Look, a people is coming from the north,
a great nation and many kings
stirred up from the farthest parts of the earth.{m}

They grasp bow and spear;
they are cruel and show no mercy.
Their sound is like the roaring sea;
they ride on horses,
arrayed as one man for battle
against you, O daughter of Babylon!

Against the one who strings the bow let the archer string his,{b}
against the one who struts in his mail.
Show no pity to her youths;
put her whole host under the ban.

Flee from the midst of Babylon;
let each one save his life!
Do not be cut off in her punishment,
for it is the time of Yahweh’s vengeance;
he is paying her what she has earned.

A golden cup was Babylon in the hand of Yahweh,
making all the earth drunk;
the nations drank of her wine;
therefore the nations went mad.

Suddenly Babylon has fallen and is shattered;
wail for her!
Take balm for her pain;
perhaps she may be healed.

Yahweh has brought forth our vindication;
come, let us tell in Zion
the work of Yahweh our God.

“Sharpen the arrows!
Fill the quivers!{c}
Yahweh has stirred up the spirit of the kings of the Medes,{d}
for his purpose concerning Babylon is to destroy it;
for it is the vengeance of Yahweh,
vengeance for his temple.

Raise a signal flag against the walls of Babylon;
strengthen the watch;
post the sentinels;
prepare the ambushes;
for Yahweh has both planned and done
what he spoke concerning the inhabitants of Babylon.

“He made the earth by his power,
established the world by his wisdom,
and by his understanding stretched out the heavens.{f}

Every man is stupid, without knowledge;
every goldsmith is put to shame by his idol,
for his cast image is a lie,
and there is no breath in them.

“A mace you are for me,{h} a tool of war:
by you I smash peoples;
by you I bring realms to ruin;

by you I smash husband and wife;
by you I smash the aged and the lad;
by you I smash the youth and the maiden;

by you I smash herdsman and herd;
by you I smash plowman and yoke of oxen;
by you I smash prefects and deputies.

“Raise a signal flag in the land;
blow the ram’s horn among the nations;
consecrate nations against her;
summon kingdoms against her,
Ararat, Minni, and Ashkenaz;{i}
appoint a marshal against her;
bring up horses like bristling locusts.

The warriors of Babylon have ceased fighting;
they sit in their strongholds;
their strength has dried up;
they have become like women.
Her dwellings are set on fire;
her bars are broken.

“He has eaten me up, Nebuchadrezzar, Babylon’s king;{k}
he has thrown me into confusion;
he has left me standing like a jar drained dry;
like a dragon he has gulped me down;
with my choice morsels he has stuffed his stomach;
he has flushed me away.

“Go out of her midst, my people!{n}
Let each one save his life
from the fierce anger of Yahweh!

For Yahweh is laying Babylon waste
and silencing her great noise;
their waves roar like many waters;
the din of their voice resounds.

Yes, a ravager has reached her—Babylon;
captured are her champions;
snapped are their bows;
for a God who requites is Yahweh;
full payment he will exact.
